## Context

Read `work/w2_stale-race/plan_v5.md` (the contract, especially its Design section), `work/w2_stale-race/builds/build.md` (the build report, including its Round 3 section), and `work/w2_stale-race/final_review_v1.md`.

The prior round fixed `cmd/bd/autoflush.go`, whose auto-import decided freshness with a hand-rolled `jsonl_content_hash` comparison blind to `jsonl_pending_hash`. Its own report flagged that `internal/autoimport.AutoImportIfNewer` still has the identical defect on its read side. That is the same bug class a second time, which means the first pass was too shallow: the plan's design makes `internal/jsonlpub` the sole authority for deciding freshness, and a hand-rolled hash comparison anywhere contradicts it.

## Scope — exactly this, nothing else

**`internal/autoimport/autoimport.go:84-97`.** `AutoImportIfNewer` reads `jsonl_content_hash` directly (with the `last_import_hash` migration fallback) and compares it to the hash of the bytes it just read. It is blind to `jsonl_pending_hash`, so in the window between a publish's rename and its promote — or after a crash there — it re-imports the database's own just-exported bytes.

Fix: make the freshness decision through `jsonlpub.ContentState`, exactly as `cmd/bd/autoflush.go` now does (read that implementation and its caller-specific mapping first; match it). Its write side already goes through `RecordImport` and must stay as it is.

Preserve every behavior that is not this defect, in particular the existing `recordImport` call on the unchanged-content path (the comment there explains it refreshes the import timestamp so a mtime-only change stops looking new) and the bd-39o migration fallback semantics, mapped onto the tri-state the same way `autoflush.go` maps them.

Add a regression test pinning the defect: with the file matching only `jsonl_pending_hash` and a different hash under `jsonl_content_hash`, `AutoImportIfNewer` must not re-import. Verify the test fails on the pre-fix tree and record that output, as the previous round did.

Then confirm the class is closed: `grep -rn 'jsonl_content_hash\|last_import_hash' --include=*.go .` excluding tests and `internal/jsonlpub` must show no remaining *freshness decision*. Two known non-defects that should remain untouched — state in your report that you checked them and why each is not a freshness decision: the daemon health check at `cmd/bd/daemon_event_loop.go:242` (tests only whether metadata is readable) and the multi-repo `updateExportMetadata` at `cmd/bd/daemon_sync.go:281` (the plan preserves multi-repo metadata byte-identical). Report anything else you find; do not fix it without saying so.

Do not make any other change. Do not add guards, tests, or refactors beyond the above.

